 "intro": "By the river Tolenus (Turano), in the land of the Marsi, 90 BC. Rome’s Italian allies have risen in the Social War. You are the consul Publius Rutilius Lupus, with Gaius Marius as your legate.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account, Rutilius and Marius built two bridges over the Tolenus. The Marsi under Vettius Scato hid in ravines near Rutilius’s bridge and ambushed his army as it crossed; Rutilius was killed with about 8,000 men, many drowned. Marius, seeing bodies floating downstream, crossed and took the Marsi camp. The Senate ordered the dead buried where they fell, to avoid panic in Rome. The other choices are what-ifs.",
